# Rona OS
#
# Leave these unset and the app runs on the invented demo data with no
# sign-in — which is exactly what the public demo deployment should do.
#
# Set both and it becomes her private app: Google sign-in, her own rows,
# everything saved. Find them in Supabase under Project Settings → API.
#
# The anon key is safe in the browser. It is not a secret — Row Level
# Security is what protects the data, and the schema enables it on every
# table. Never put the service_role key here.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---- Her mailbox ----
# One app password per inbox, created by her at
# myaccount.google.com/apppasswords (needs 2-Step Verification on).
#
# Never commit this file with values in it, and never paste the code
# into chat or email — 1Password is what it is for.
#
# Spaces in the 16-character code are ignored.

GMAIL_USER=
GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=
